    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d112">

                <pb facs="0147" n="131" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg131"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.113/11–3047: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Venezuela</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Maleady</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-11-30T12:00:00-04:30">November 30,
                            1947—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>466. Betancourt<anchor n="1" xml:id="d112-f1"/> called in heads Creole,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d112-f2"/> Shell Oil<anchor n="3" xml:id="d112-f3"/> companies
                    last night. Told them has unimpeachable evidence Brazil sold 5,000 automatic
                    rifles, 2,000,000 shells therefor to Dominican Government. Said Trujillo<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d112-f4"/> yacht with Dominican Ministry War official aboard
                    touched Trinidad day or two ago presumably en route Brazil pick up arms. Also
                    said Venezuelan Government much concerned since convinced arms destined attempt
                    oust it.</p>
                <p>Betancourt went on to say he has told Brazil if arms deal not cancelled he will
                    stop all shipments crude oil refined products there. Inasmuch as we principal
                    supplier oil and latter cannot be obtained elsewhere, Brazil is expected
                    capitulate. If not, he told oil heads, he will ask them cooperate by stopping
                    shipments.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">El País</hi> reported today Trujillo’s yacht en route
                    Brazil pick up arms.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 466, repeated Rio de Janeiro and Ciudad Trujillo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Maleady</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d112-f1" n="1" xml:id="d112-f1-content">
                <p>Romulo Betancourt, President of the Revolutionary Junta of Government.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d112-f2" n="2" xml:id="d112-f2-content">
                <p>Creole Petroleum Corporation, Holding Company for the Interests of Standard Oil
                    Company of New Jersey in Venezuela.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d112-f3" n="3" xml:id="d112-f3-content">
                <p>Royal Dutch Shell Company.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d112-f4" n="4" xml:id="d112-f4-content">
                <p>Rafael Leonidas Trujillo, President of the Dominican Republic.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
